{"title":"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2025 AMC 10B #2</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2025 AMC 12B #2</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Slightly_more_rigorous_than_Solution_1,_but_same_idea)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Slightly more rigorous than Solution 1, but same idea)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Similar_to_the_other_solutions_but_without_the_use_of_mods)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Similar to the other solutions but without the use of mods)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4:_Modular_Arithmetic;_Ultra-Rigorous,_Not_Recommended\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4: Modular Arithmetic; Ultra-Rigorous, Not Recommended</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:30)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:30)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jerry wrote down the ones digit of each of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> positive squares: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fca82f52d9ac4dba30fb01eead0c7665e308c9e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 4, 9, 6, 5, 6, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"17\" />. What is the sum of all the numbers Jerry wrote down?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/696e9b892c9ab1a27a118e10e8f34f71c428337f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~9025 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}~9070 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}~9090 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}~9115 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}~9160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"487\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By a modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> argument, the ones digits repeat with period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in the following order:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99bbc84180fd0cff1b24f3718fe818b79805bf23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1,4,9,6,5,6,9,4,1,0\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"16\" />\nThe sum of the numbers can be verified to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594b4629a09e61341c38216de1aa1fa8f7ee44a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$202$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> periods that occur from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and there are five extra numbers, those being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f08e0e246ee85bb5df156ee9feb418b562e49e31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,4,9,6,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />, corresponding to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74d469d22bdb3c984af408903c44687438f5240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2021,2022,2023,2024,2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"17\" />. The sum of these numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, the total is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8858bf3b36a3aaefdf551cd8101aa8a7fc175da7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[202\\cdot 45+25=9090+25=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~9115}\\]\" width=\"306\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p><p>~ Phinetium\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Slightly_more_rigorous_than_Solution_1.2C_but_same_idea.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Slightly_more_rigorous_than_Solution_1,_but_same_idea)\">Solution 2 (Slightly more rigorous than Solution 1, but same idea)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Slightly more rigorous than Solution 1, but same idea)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/9213a37f4783ba3160e06bb782796e57a8bf745c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\equiv n\\quad\\textrm{(mod 10)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/368ad410190a4cd452ca94ceaafe5a4a96295f6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2\\equiv n^2\\quad\\textrm{(mod 10)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"21\" />. So, the numbers must repeat in patterns of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Listing them out gives:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/482d4b1a33a20404cbd4ce8cb9492b1202efffe0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1,4,9,6,5,6,9,4,1,0.\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"16\" />These numbers sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509a9369d5c55fd98dc99cb2938fb44f0101f90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2020$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/9/c09b65d45ee039041735fcd1f8a1b48865efbf20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45\\cdot202=9090$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"14\" />. Since we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more numbers, we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf7f09a30a4c645a8f3a6e1cd085a7762af374c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+4+9+6+5=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"179\" height=\"15\" /> to our answer to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43a42d26d1c39878b1dfee9b22ceeffb423cf62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~9115}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"85\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Franklin2013\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Similar_to_the_other_solutions_but_without_the_use_of_mods.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Similar_to_the_other_solutions_but_without_the_use_of_mods)\">Solution 3 (Similar to the other solutions but without the use of mods)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Similar to the other solutions but without the use of mods)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ones digit of a square number is determined by the ones digit of the base.  \nWe can find the pattern by looking at the ones digits of the first ten positive squares:\n</p><p>\\begin{aligned}\n1^2 &amp;= 1 \\\\\n2^2 &amp;= 4 \\\\\n3^2 &amp;= 9 \\\\\n4^2 &amp;= 16 \\quad (\\text{ones digit } 6) \\\\\n5^2 &amp;= 25 \\quad (\\text{ones digit } 5) \\\\\n6^2 &amp;= 36 \\quad (\\text{ones digit } 6) \\\\\n7^2 &amp;= 49 \\quad (\\text{ones digit } 9) \\\\\n8^2 &amp;= 64 \\quad (\\text{ones digit } 4) \\\\\n9^2 &amp;= 81 \\quad (\\text{ones digit } 1) \\\\\n10^2 &amp;= 100 \\quad (\\text{ones digit } 0)\n\\end{aligned}\n</p><p><br />\nThe sequence of ones digits is:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>This pattern of ten digits repeats for every subsequent group of ten squares (e.g., \\(11^2\\) has the same ones digit as \\(1^2\\), \\(12^2\\) as \\(2^2\\), etc.).\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p><br />\nWe now divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as the pattern repeats every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />/<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594b4629a09e61341c38216de1aa1fa8f7ee44a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$202$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> full cycles with a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594b4629a09e61341c38216de1aa1fa8f7ee44a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$202$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> full cycles is:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594b4629a09e61341c38216de1aa1fa8f7ee44a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$202$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> * <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a6ed311694f85c3a50f0018a200efd0dd75d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9090$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> \n</p><p><br />\nHowever, we must add back <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits, as we had a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when we divided <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the sum of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits is:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p><br />\nThus, the total sum is:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29a6ed311694f85c3a50f0018a200efd0dd75d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9090$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bcef9d7c9b5b77bbd0a83d1b07d6d1a79e3b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9115$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43a42d26d1c39878b1dfee9b22ceeffb423cf62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~9115}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"85\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~BryBro7\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4:_Modular_Arithmetic.3B_Ultra-Rigorous.2C_Not_Recommended\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4:_Modular_Arithmetic;_Ultra-Rigorous,_Not_Recommended\">Solution 4: Modular Arithmetic; Ultra-Rigorous, Not Recommended</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4: Modular Arithmetic; Ultra-Rigorous, Not Recommended\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want the sum of the ones digits of \n\\( 1^2, 2^2, 3^2, \\ldots, 2025^2 \\). The normal way is to notice the pattern repeats every 10, but instead we will approach this with more modular arithmetic than any sane person would tolerate.\n</p><p>Let \\( f(n) = n^2 \\mod 10 \\), which extracts the ones digit of \\( n^2 \\).\nWe want\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa9d504a36b657076115375f0272e7a61008666c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\sum_{n=1}^{2025} f(n).\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>First observe the basic periodicity result:\nSince \\( n^2 \\mod 10 \\) depends only on \\( n \\mod 10 \\), we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/8/0584ea1ce3fbfa66dc92af2caef48d9d892bc9d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n+10) \\equiv f(n) \\pmod{10}.\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We will pretend this is deep.\n</p><p>Now compute all residues \\( n \\mod 10 \\) and their corresponding \\( n^2 \\mod 10 \\):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5cda6f17a9460c0659d14c3b85446dcf32d3de0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c c} 0^2 &amp; \\equiv 0 \\\\ 1^2 &amp; \\equiv 1 \\\\ 2^2 &amp; \\equiv 4 \\\\ 3^2 &amp; \\equiv 9 \\\\ 4^2 &amp; \\equiv 6 \\\\ 5^2 &amp; \\equiv 5 \\\\ 6^2 &amp; \\equiv 6 \\\\ 7^2 &amp; \\equiv 9 \\\\ 8^2 &amp; \\equiv 4 \\\\ 9^2 &amp; \\equiv 1. \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"195\" />\n</p><p>Instead of immediately summing these, we treat the 10-term sequence as a modular function over the ring \\( \\mathbb{Z}/10\\mathbb{Z} \\).\nDefine the sequence \\( a_k = (k^2 \\mod 10) \\) for \\( k \\in \\mathbb{Z}/10\\mathbb{Z} \\).\nWe want the sum\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635d6e0e873864c7cd08129bb397b5cd56def820.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[T = \\sum_{k=0}^9 a_k = 0 + 1 + 4 + 9 + 6 + 5 + 6 + 9 + 4 + 1 = 45.\\]\" width=\"445\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>Next, determine how many full cycles of length 10 lie in the first 2025 integers.\nCompute\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c605312b94f3abe1ca5af1fd89c94d9f4f4cab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2025 \\mod 10 \\equiv 5.\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/294412d187142d36496b156e18bd174e13e4a04b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2025 = 10 \\cdot 202 + 5.\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>So we have 202 complete cycles plus 5 extra terms.\n</p><p>Sum contributed by the full cycles:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b2e2040aabf42df1ede3411327152787acff6f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[202 \\cdot 45.\\]\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>We now compute this entirely modulo 10 even though we need the actual sum.\nFirst,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79e3505d014b365f7f9449a3285787d85f23b5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[202 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{10}, \\quad 45 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{10},\\]\" width=\"323\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da4c1dc75e589ee4c1544ea2828542d1c8036bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[202 \\cdot 45 \\equiv 2 \\cdot 5 = 10 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{10}.\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This tells us nothing useful, so abandon that and compute normally:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35042b8be713aa19613fb8375d1fa9beadcc38d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[202 \\cdot 45 = (200 \\cdot 45) + (2 \\cdot 45) = 9000 + 90 = 9090.\\]\" width=\"396\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now handle the leftover 5 terms: \\( n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 \\).\nCompute \\( n^2 \\mod 10 \\) again even though we already have it:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b647b882fcc54e9f9200b3f825031ab932e56e79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1^2 \\equiv 1, \\quad 2^2 \\equiv 4, \\quad 3^2 \\equiv 9, \\quad 4^2 \\equiv 6, \\quad 5^2 \\equiv 5.\\]\" width=\"350\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Sum:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a79318b0cbc105203b9c368461ef6221f3f8c653.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + 4 + 9 + 6 + 5 = 25.\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The full sum is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/81954765fca5087fc8e5d95750c9a7cdcf87c393.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = 9090 + 25 = 9115.\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>To unnecessarily verify using modular decomposition, write\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b67c7a862aa9a0cf1f898c34627bff4373db3bf3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S \\equiv \\sum_{n=1}^{2025} n^2 \\pmod{10}.\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>We can compute the entire sum of squares formula modulo 10 and compare.\nUsing\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f014f842db0e9fa2be57a941082b7df0f0987bd7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=1}^N n^2 = \\frac{N(N+1)(2N+1)}{6},\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>take \\( N = 2025 \\).\nReduce everything modulo 10 first:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6e921deab92816a4bd095df16d58d8c00cd7688.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2025 \\equiv 5, \\quad 2026 \\equiv 6, \\quad 4051 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{10}.\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now compute\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c240a5d9ebba36102f351c4c7ce7dc096ecfae9a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 1 = 30.\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d6412e9b431ad6261131af787c6ce90e0f622fb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=1}^{2025} n^2 \\equiv 30 \\cdot 6^{-1} \\pmod{10}.\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Compute the inverse of 6 modulo 10.\nSolve \\( 6x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{10} \\).\nNo such \\( x \\) exists because \\( \\gcd(6, 10) = 2 \\neq 1 \\).\nTherefore this modular-verification method is unusable, so we immediately stop and simply trust the earlier cycle-counting method.\n</p><p>Thus the sum of the ones digits of the first 2025 squares is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cd2225bdd51491565d51340dc8b00df7cb9a80e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9115.\\]\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>~notvalid\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E0:30.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~0:30)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:30)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~0:30)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/gFNczjnj2DY\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/gFNczjnj2DY</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s-Wimgu9wto\">https://youtu.be/s-Wimgu9wto</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Simple)\">Video Solution(Quick and Simple)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Simple)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G4oCT4o3Ues\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G4oCT4o3Ues</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jxSb3BIzKJg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jxSb3BIzKJg</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLSWVrrKsgs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B\">2025 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\